# D2 (R-140 item 2, user-approved 2026-10-26): the +-64 vs +-128 box check. P128 = c110_2x2/CD.par (rp10, comoving,
# production DE, L4-equivalent, base8 6ea832af, GPU IPC off) with the box doubled to +-128: root nx unchanged (128),
# so the root dx doubles (1 -> 2), plus one more level (num_levels 5 -> 6) so the finest dx (1/16) is unchanged.
# Level-indexed keys moved up by one (levels are relative to the root, dyngr_tov.cpp:1055): refined_region1/2 level,
# amr_level_bh, amr_level_debris (dyngr_tov.cpp:580-581). Length keys are in M and unchanged: amr_buffer (= one finest
# block width, 16/16 = 1 M at either level count), amr_radius_bh, zone, excision, frame controller, ADM radii.
# mg_norm_ref_volume stays 128^3 deliberately: it fixes the MG l2/rms defect normalisation independently of the box
# (multigrid_driver.cpp:1098-1102, multigrid.hpp:654-658), so the solve tolerance is the same as in CD.
# Window t 0 -> 80 (pre-periapsis); compared with CD's own history over the same window.
# 2x2 arm CD (R-123 Q3 / R-124 item 3; PREPARED -- start only after the user approves the output plan):
# rp10, L4, t 0 -> 200, base8 (proj/tde 6ea832af), GPU IPC off (tde_mpi_env.sh), fresh start. Comoving gauge (frame controller), PRODUCTION dual energy.
# Derived from ref7/R6_u.par (the R6 = rp10 production deck) by c110_mk.py.
# LAUNCH ENVIRONMENT (R-122, 2026-10-25): GPU IPC OFF -- MPIR_CVAR_CH4_IPC_GPU_P2P_THRESHOLD=2147483647 MPIR_CVAR_CH4_IPC_MAP_REPEAT_ADDR=0
# (source athenak_run/cfc/tde_mpi_env.sh); IPC on crashes AMR runs after many regrids (research/notes/GPU_IPC_CRASH.md).
# R6 (r_p = 10) production deck, derived from R7_rp18_comov_L4_zone.par by the code session (C-100,
# R-112 item 6): R6 orbit (star_vel from the X11 deck), zone r_s = 5, tlim 170, dcycle 250; every key
# whose default changed is explicit.
# R7 (rp18, comoving, L4, zone) production deck. Base: RC_R7T/parfile.par (R-076 item 6 recheck T arm)
# plus the R7 shell fix F1 + F2 (C-072; added to production decks per the user, 2026-10-20). proj/tde >= d8635dae.
# plus the AMR debris buffer + hysteresis (C-075/C-076; production per the user, 2026-10-21). proj/tde >= 6b02cffb.
# Running zone production itself still needs the user's approval.
# R-063/R-064 S2 (user-approved 2026-10-14), arm T: zone on + covariant (+ tier 3, rule-gated). Restart of R7 (si = 0 production deck);
# window per R-063 §5. Phase timers on (default).
# C-041 item 7 (user-approved 2026-10-12): rp18 (Q3's star velocity) in the comoving gauge,
# remnant-targeting controller (tracking radius 3 M around the pinned target), BH box L4, to t = 300;
# otherwise = R6_rp10_comov_L4_fix (item 6 deck + solve_interval = 0).
# R-040 item 6 (Milestone 2 test 2): rp10 (the Q1 deck) in the comoving gauge with the xidot
# controller (athenak a55466a0, corrected trumpet Ahat0 per item 77, psi^6 capped inside r_iso 0.3 M), star pinned at the origin, BH released from x = -30,
# BH box at L4, star/debris L4, to t = 200. Trumpet Ahat0 now carries psi^6 (item 77,
# user decision): the Q1 comparison mixes gauge + K fix; K77_q1_rst5 isolates the K effect.
# prod_ensemble1 member: parabolic TDE scan, design periapsis R_areal=10 r_g (E=1),
# solve_interval=1 (calibration: L drift 6x smaller than si=10). IC from
# scripts/tde_parabolic_orbit_ic.py --x0 30 --periapsis 10. Otherwise = cfc_tde_wd_imbh_parabolic_tracker.athinput.
# PARABOLIC-ORBIT variant of cfc_tde_wd_imbh_elliptic_tracker.athinput.
# Same WD (TOV rhoc/kappa/Gamma=5/3, M_*=7.47e-5 = 0.75 Msun), same IMBH
# (puncture_mass=1.0 = 1e4 Msun), same release point (30,0,0) = 1.83 r_t, same
# DESIGN periapsis R_areal=10.0 r_g (penetration beta = r_t/r_p = 1.64), same mesh
# and region-tracker AMR. ONLY the orbit changes: Killing energy E=1 (marginally
# bound) instead of the elliptic E=0.976865.
#
# ORBIT. scripts/tde_parabolic_orbit_ic.py. For E=1 the Schwarzschild turning-point
# condition gives L^2 = 2 r_p^2/(r_p-2) exactly, so L=5 (elliptic: 4.391). Released at
# finite x0 the star is already falling in, so unlike the elliptic case the velocity
# has a RADIAL part and the shift enters the energy, E = alpha W - beta^i p_i
# (beta^i p_i = -2.78e-4 here; identically zero in the elliptic case). Stage A
# (closed form) and Stage B (geodesic integrated in the real trumpet gauge) agree on
# the periapsis to 7e-9 r_g. Design periapsis at t=135.9, at (x,y)=(-6.61,6.07).
#
# !! THE DESIGN PERIAPSIS IS NOT WHAT THE SIMULATION ACHIEVES. Measured in the
# elliptic production run (tde_prod_fixed_v3 + its parent v2): E and L are exactly
# the design values at t=0 (to 1e-4 -- the IC pipeline is correct), but L then decays
# ~0.015-0.02%/M during infall, 4.9% by t=250, before any disruption, with E drifting down
# alongside: a numerical DRAG. The achieved periapsis was R_areal=6.8 at t=364, not
# 10.0 at t=349. Cause not yet identified. The parabolic infall is ~2.6x shorter, so
# the shortfall should be smaller, but it must be MEASURED (calibration stage of the
# plan) before this deck is used for production.
#
# PRODUCTION RECIPE folded in (NANCASCADE_HANDOFF.md Sec 19.2/20.2), which the parent
# in-repo input predates: excision (lapse scheme), psi_floor, src_nan_check, ADM-mass
# surface integrals. Binary must contain the Sec 15 grad_ap6_0 fix (d9166815) and the
# region tracker (bdc42eb1).
#
# AMR. Region tracker (rho > amr_density_frac*rho_max) UNIONED with the fixed puncture
# box -- the configuration validated on 16 nodes to t=145 in
# tde_tracker_nexteval_longrun_v1. CAVEAT: that validation was on the RADIAL deck
# (+-32 box, level 5, every-substage solves); this is its first use on the elliptic/
# parabolic deck (+-64, level 4, solve_interval=10), and nothing has yet run the
# region tracker past t~150 cleanly (the second_deriv arm hung at t=150.9; the
# region-only control, job 8912718, will tell whether that is second_deriv-specific).

<comment>
problem  = Parabolic-orbit TDE (E=1, r_p=10 r_g design), region-tracker AMR, excision

<job>
restart_state = true   # C-100: bitwise restarts (w0, flags, MG warm starts in the restart; needs proj/tde >= eefaf908)
basename = cfc_tde_wd_imbh_parabolic_tracker

<mesh>
# Same cubic power-of-2 root grid as the parent fixture (see its header for why):
# 128/16=8 root MeshBlocks/axis, multigrid root hierarchy halves cleanly to 1x1x1.
nghost = 4        # Number of ghost cells
nx1    = 128      # 8 MeshBlocks in x1-direction (root level), dx=1.0
x1min  = -128.0    # minimum x1
x1max  = 128.0     # maximum x1 -- orbit stays within +/-30, ample buffer beyond
ix1_bc = diode    # inner boundary -- full domain, no reflection symmetry
ox1_bc = diode    # outer boundary

nx2    = 128      # 8 MeshBlocks in x2-direction (root level), dx=1.0
x2min  = -128.0    # minimum x2
x2max  = 128.0     # maximum x2
ix2_bc = diode    # inner boundary
ox2_bc = diode    # outer boundary

nx3    = 128      # 8 MeshBlocks in x3-direction (root level), dx=1.0
x3min  = -128.0    # minimum x3
x3max  = 128.0     # maximum x3
ix3_bc = diode    # inner boundary
ox3_bc = diode    # outer boundary

<meshblock>
nx1  = 16        # must be a power of 2 (multigrid requirement)
nx2  = 16
nx3  = 16

<mesh_refinement>
refinement          = adaptive  # was static -- see header note on the SetNeighbors risk
max_nmb_per_rank    = 400
num_levels          = 6         # D2: +1 level (finest dx 1/16 unchanged)
refinement_interval = 1
ncycle_check        = 1         # check every cycle -- the star moves far less than
                                 # one level-4 block-width per cycle (v0=0.1357c *
                                 # dt~0.03), comfortably fast enough to keep up.

<amr_criterion0>
method = user           # dispatches to TDERefineTracker (dyngr_tov.cpp), enrolled
                        # via <problem> amr_condition=tde_track below.

# Two static SEED boxes (puncture + star's t=0 position), not the full disk the
# static fixture uses -- required, not redundant with adaptive: there is no
# initial-AMR pass, and CheckForRefinement's cooldown means adaptive alone would
# take several cycles to reach level 4 from the root grid, during which the star
# (R_*=0.677) would sit under-resolved (same reasoning as cfc_tde_wd_imbh_amr.
# athinput). TDERefineTracker maintains/moves both boxes thereafter.
<refined_region1>
level = 5  # D2 (was 4): puncture, fixed at the origin
x1min = -32.0
x1max = -28.0
x2min = -2.0
x2max = 2.0
x3min = -2.0
x3max = 2.0

<refined_region2>
level = 5        # D2 (was 4): star, at its t=0 position
x1min = -3.0
x1max = 3.0
x2min = -3.0
x2max = 3.0
x3min = -2.0
x3max = 2.0

<time>
dt_limiter_report_every = 500   # R-115 Q3c: periodic DTLIM/DTRHO report (needs proj/tde base5)
evolution  = dynamic    # dynamic/kinematic/static
gr_dt      = true
dt_skip_excised = true   # item 73 (user-approved for V5): excised cells out of the CFL
io_timers = true
dt_floor_keep_velocity = true   # R7 shell fix F2 (C-072; production per the user 2026-10-20)
integrator = rk3        # time integration algorithm
cfl_number = 0.4
nlim       = -1
tlim = 80   # D2 window
                         # the elliptic run's ~150 M post-periapsis window. Star CoM
                         # at r_iso~33 by then (Stage B); the unbound debris tip
                         # reaches the +-64 boundary somewhat later -- extend only
                         # after checking where the debris actually is.
ndiag      = 1          # cycles between diagnostic output

<coord>
general_rel = true      # general relativity
m           = 1.0
a           = 0.0
excise      = true      # NANCASCADE Sec 17/19: removes the unexcised-puncture
                        # pile-up that killed every no-excision run at t~445
excision_scheme = lapse # NOT fixed: rexcise is hardcoded to 1.0, and M_BH grows by
                        # accretion, so only a lapse surface tracks it (Sec 13.1)
excise_lapse    = 0.25
excision_radius_dynamic = true    # R-112 item 3 time-dependent excision: R7 x2.12 (C-100); R6 neutral, on for uniformity (R-113 Q3)
excision_rmax = 2.5
excision_margin_cells = 4
excision_vin = 0.6
excision_rho_thr = 3.24e-14        # = <mhd> atmosphere_zone_rho (1e-10 rho_c)
excision_mask_refresh = true   # R-076 item 6 recheck (user-approved 2026-10-18)
dexcise     = 1.0e-24   # = <mhd> dfloor
texcise     = 1.0e-22   # = <mhd> tfloor

<mhd>
mass_closure = true          # R-114 MCLOSE: itemized rest-mass closure per segment (needs proj/tde >= 4e3bbf20)
mass_closure_mstar = 7.5e-5   # M* in code units (R-114: 1e-10 M* = 7.5e-15)
mass_closure_tol = 1.0e-10    # pass: |R| <= tol M* per segment
mass_closure_every = 0        # per-cycle MCLOSE_CYC lines (debug; 0 = off)
mass_closure_full = true      # R-115 Q5: SCLOSE1/2/3 + ECLOSE (S_i, tau closures; needs base5)
nscalars = 1
dual_energy_diag = true          # R-044 §4 item 2: switch maps (K_en/K_tr, flagged fraction)
dual_energy = true                # V5 (user-approved): F + J + second-law guard (items 71-73), L4
dual_energy_kmax = 1.0
dual_energy_rho_switch = 3.2e-8
# R-087 item 4 (user-approved 2026-10-23): explicit tracer-flux, FOFC and cold-recovery keys,
# so no default change or solver change can silently revert them. Needs proj/tde >= cc441bb5.
dual_energy_flux = hll            # the tracer's flux: HLL flux of D*Y (hlle_dyn_grmhd.hpp)
scalar_flux_hll = true            # every scalar (here only the tracer) through that same code
dual_energy_recon_rhoy = true     # reconstruct rho*Y, Y_face = (rho Y)_face/rho_face
fofc_scalar_consistent = true     # FOFC faces: scalar flux = 1st-order Riemann flux of D*Y
cold_recovery = true              # T < tfloor, rho not floored: prims from D, S_i (C-083/C-085)
fofc_cold_recovery = true         # the FOFC probe counts cold-recoverable cells as good
eos         = ideal      # EOS type
dyn_eos     = ideal      # EOS type
dyn_error   = reset_floor # error policy
reconstruct = ppmx       # spatial reconstruction method
rsolver     = hlle       # Riemann solver to be used
dfloor      = 1.0e-24    # atmosphere floor (as requested)
tfloor      = 1.0e-22    # matches the established 100x-above-dfloor ratio
dthreshold  = 1.02       # Threshold for flooring
gamma       = 1.6666666666666667  # 5/3, per the WD-like polytrope
dyn_scratch = 1
fofc        = true
enforce_maximum = false

atmosphere_frame_velocity = true
atmosphere_frame_gate = 6.0
dual_energy_div = covariant
dual_energy_flag_exchange = true    # (A), explicit (the code default is also true)
dual_energy_shock_counters = 100    # R-112 item 1 DESHK lines every N cycles (0 = off); R-115 Q3c: on
atmosphere_zone = true
atmosphere_zone_unmask = true   # R7 shell fix F1 (C-072; production per the user 2026-10-20; needs proj/tde >= d8635dae)
atmosphere_zone_radius = 5      # min(6, 0.5 r_p), r_p = 10
atmosphere_zone_rho = 3.24e-14    # 1e-10 rho_c
atmosphere_zone_vmax = 0.9
atmosphere_zone_tier3 = true      # R-058 §3 rule (R-063 §3); tier3_rho default 1e-16 rho_c
mass_ledger = true   # R-076 item 6: closure row (<= 1e-10 M* per segment)

<adm>
<cfc>
init_verbose = true
init_omega   = 1.0
# Same production-validated CFC solver settings as the parent fixture (see its
# header for the full measurement trail): mg_threshold/mg_poisson_threshold=1e-8,
# mg_poisson_mporder=2, mg_npresmooth/npostsmooth=2, mg_norm=rms (R3). Unrelated to
# the velocity boost -- accuracy of these settings is independent of star_vel_x2.
mg_threshold   = 1.0e-8
mg_poisson_threshold = 1.0e-8
mg_poisson_mporder = 2
mg_npresmooth  = 2
mg_npostsmooth = 2
mg_norm = rms
mg_norm_ref_volume = 2097152.0  # C-040 P3: 128^3 (= this box: bitwise no-op, box-independent threshold)
puncture_enabled = true
puncture_mass    = 1.0            # M_BH = 1e4 Msun, fixed at the coordinate origin
# alpha_floor: REQUIRED -- default 0.0 clamps a negative lapse to EXACTLY zero,
# causing a 1/alpha singularity/NANS_IN_CONS cascade near the puncture (item 59).
alpha_floor = 1.0e-6
# psi_floor: clamp at the psi SOLVE OUTPUT, before AssembleConformalMetric and before
# the ghost exchange (CFC::ApplyPsiFloor). Hardening, validated non-regressing.
psi_floor   = 1.0e-6
# solve_interval: same production-validated cadence as the static-region fixture
# (DEVELOPMENT.md item 61/62) -- 3.65x speedup, negligible accuracy cost.
# Independent of TDERefineTracker, which locates the star directly from
# pmhd->w0's density every check, not from any CFC-solved quantity.
solve_interval = 0  # C-041 fix: metric solved every RK stage (once-per-step solves heat a comoving star: T3_si0 vs D_a)
# Names the first non-finite elliptic source/output instead of a silent cascade.
# One branch when clean. Fires only on solve cycles (every 10th here).
src_nan_check = 1
# ADM-mass surface integrals: the only INDEPENDENT check that the mass
# AccreteExcisedMass hands the puncture really appears in the spacetime (item 57).
adm_mass_r0 = 20.0
adm_mass_r1 = 30.0
adm_mass_r2 = 40.0
puncture_moving = true
puncture_x1 = -30.0
puncture_x2 = 0.0
puncture_x3 = 0.0
frame_controller = true
frame_track_rho = 3.24e-5
frame_track_radius = 3.0
frame_tau_x = 20.0
frame_tau_a = 2.0
frame_atm_rho = 1.0e-22
frame_atm_gate = 6.0
<problem>
isotropic   = true      # required: CFC solves for the isotropic-gauge metric AND
                         # is required by star_vel_x1/2/3 (see dyngr_tov.cpp)
rhoc        = 3.24e-4   # converted from 3.24e-12 (Msun=1 units) via lambda^2
kappa       = 1.2346626297e-2  # converted from 2.66e3 (Msun=1 units) via lambda^(-4/3)
npoints     = 10000.0   # buffer points for TOV calculation
dr          = 2e-4      # npoints*dr = 2.0, ~3x the star's own R_*=0.677
b_norm      = 0.0       # unmagnetized
pcut        = 1e-6
magindex    = 1
star_center_x1 = 0.0  # ~1.83x the tidal radius (r_t=16.4) -- release point
star_center_x2 = 0.0     # puncture always fixed at the origin
star_center_x3 = 0.0
star_vel_x1    = -0.19262227  # PARABOLIC ORBIT (E=1, L=5), r_p = 10 (R6; RC_R6X11/X11 deck values)
star_vel_x2    =   0.15093084
star_vel_x3    =  0.0         # scripts/tde_parabolic_orbit_ic.py --x0 30 --periapsis 10
user_hist   = true       # enrolls TOVHistory (rho-max, alpha-min)
amr_condition   = tde_track   # enrolls TDERefineTracker -- THE feature this
                                # fixture exists to test.
amr_radius_bh   = 2.0          # fine box around the fixed puncture
amr_density_frac = 1.0e-2      # debris region: rho > amr_density_frac*rho_max
amr_level_bh = 5   # D2 (was 4): finest dx 1/16 unchanged
amr_level_debris = 5   # D2 (was 4)
amr_buffer = 1.0        # C-075/C-076 (production per the user 2026-10-21): one level-4 block width
amr_deref_frac = 1.0e-3  # C-075/C-076: hysteresis, derefine 10x below the refine cut

<output1>
file_type   = hst      # History data dump -- mass/momentum/energy conservation check
dt          = 0.1
data_format = %20.15e

<output2>
file_type   = bin      # Binary output -- psi/alpha near the puncture and star
variable    = adm
dt = 2.0   # output plan: slices every 2 M
slice_x3    = 0.0
id = adm_xy

<output3>
file_type   = bin      # Binary output -- density, to follow the star and its debris
variable    = mhd_w_bcc
dt = 2.0   # output plan: slices every 2 M
slice_x3    = 0.0
id = prim_xy

<output4>
file_type   = rst      # Restart dumps -- ~29,000 cycles (2.5x the parent's
dcycle = 500   # output plan: restarts every 500 cycles; milestones kept

<output5>
file_type   = bin      # R-044 §4 item 2: dual-energy switch maps, orbital plane
variable    = mhd_de_diag
dt = 2.0   # output plan: slices every 2 M
slice_x3    = 0.0
id = dediag_xy

# R-115 Q3c reference-run outputs: xz slices (rho, v, K and the dual-energy maps) and 3D
# primitives every 6 M (covers periapsis and t_end in both windows)
<output6>
file_type   = bin
variable    = mhd_w_bcc
dt = 2.0   # output plan: slices every 2 M
slice_x2    = 0.0
id = prim_xz

<output7>
file_type   = bin
variable    = mhd_de_diag
dt = 2.0   # output plan: slices every 2 M
slice_x2    = 0.0
id = dediag_xz

<output8>
file_type   = bin
variable    = mhd_w_bcc
dt = 12.0   # output plan: 3D every 12 M
id = prim_3d

<output9>
file_type   = bin
variable    = mhd_w_bcc
dt          = 135.9   # output plan: the periapsis 3D dump (design periapsis)
id = prim_3d_peri
